"Perhaps we are at the forefront points in the world in the number of lejsters for tax returns," notes Karel Havlíček of the Association of Small and Medium-Sized Enterprises and Crafts of the Czech Republic.
Simpluing entrepreneurship in recent years has become a prosecuted target of all governments.
Compared to the world, however, the situation in the Czech Republic does not particularly improve.
According to the World Bank, the Czech Republic ranks 74th in terms of conditions for entrepreneurship, which is eight places worse than last year.
The Absurdity of the Year competition was first pronounced in 2006 and takes place every year according to the same scenario.
Anyone can submit administrative and bureaucratic nonsense every year from April to the end of September, when there is a deadline for the competition.
The web address www.firmaroku.cz Then the organizer of the competition selects seven nominees for the "anti-ecliner" and will be voted by the public via the Internet during October at www.firmaroku.cz/absurdita and www.ihned.cz.
Absurdity, which gets the most vote wins.
More than a Hundred have been applied for this year's poll this year, more precisely 105 prescriptions and deceiver meaning.
These tips were sent by entrepreneurs, as well as professional federations and reporters.
Among the "finalists" of the competition there was, for example, a requirement between the nominees that cars for the maintenance of motorways and expressways pay to tolls, entrepreneurs with twenty employees, two offices and two toilets every two years.
A list of this year's seven designs is published on the competition's website.
Announcement of the competition, which always takes place at the beginning of November on Wenceslas Square in Prague, is part of hapenning, which is regularly attended by the personality of political and societal life.
This year, for example, this culmination of the competition was assisted by Eva Svobodová, Director of the Association of Small and Medium-sized Enterprises and Crafts of the Czech Republic or Petr Kužel, President of the Chamber of Commerce of the Czech Republic.
"Economic prosperity can't work where the state is throwing sticks under entrepreneurs, so my goal is to abolish at least three-dozen sections every year, composing entrepreneurship unnecessarily every year," Minister of Industry and Commerce Martin Kocourek said.
Elections to abolish nonsensical regulations do not sound empty.
In 2007, people were most annoyed by the businessman's obligation to report three days to the Trade Licensing Office in the place where there is a permanent establishment, the intention to go with a booth for an exhibition or a pilgrimage.
This obligation has been eliminated by an amendment to the Trade Licensing Act.
The second most-voted obligation in 2007, in which the reporting of the Labor Office on behalf of its foreign employee was a business trip of up to 30 days was eliminated by the so-called Green Card Act.
And for the third time everything good.
The absurdity of 2009 became the regulation of physiotherapists to have a large mirror, a refrigerator and two treadmill in the office.
It was mitigated this year by the decree of the Ministry of Health - the obligation to have a refrigerator fell away.
The new category acknowledging companies
Ecological, humanitarian, educational and sporting projects are evaluated.
A novelty in this year's fifth edition of Hospodářské noviny competitions is a category called Responsible Firm of the Year 2010.
The mission of this competition is to promote a sensuous and fair entrepreneurship.
"We in this way support companies that take into account the impact of their business on the environment and support socially responsible activities," says Patrik Bartholdy, a regional mobile operator's regional mobile operator, which is an announcer and guarantor of the competition, as well as in the case of a rebel-of-year competition.
This year’s first-legged sub-category of the main Vodafone Firm of the Year 2010 competition has been entered by companies for which success in business is not the only long-lasting goal.
The story of each of them is very inspirational and he would go on a standalone article.
Although they differ diametrically the subject of their activities from each other, the common denunciators of their endeavor can be considered support and consideration.
In one case it applies, for example, to disabled people and, for example, personal problems or the health of their own employees.
Fourteen nation-wide finalists include, for example, the Prague software company Et Netera, which supports the creation of informal sports teams among employees, who then take part in a number of tournaments in various sports.
A different example of a responsible company from the Pardubice Region is Isolit-Bravo, which for seventeen years is the main contributor of an endowment fund sponsoring handicapped children.
Its disabled employees are taken care of by a paper mill from Poděbrady, which has more than 70 percent of them, and therefore it received the title of Responsible Firm of the Central Bohemian Region and in the Vodafone Company of the Year competition it ranked third in the region.
The accounting firm MiRyz Soft, which introduced flexible working hours, also minatured to an average of 35 hours a week, won in the Olomouc region, but not proportionately reduced schedules.
The jurty-sufficient jury has also awarded her for preferentially buying from Czech manufacturers, supporting civic activities in the vicinity and saving the environment.
"We try to recycle as much as possible so that our business and our administration have the slightest impact on the environment as possible," explains Managing Director Miluše Ryznarová.
Responsible IT company Enlogit from the Usti Region thinks about the health of its employees and bought them ergonomic chairs and keyboards for each laptop, supports their work from home and at its corporate events uses catering services provided by a local sheltered workshop.
"Finally, we are supporting the People in Need Foundation, which specifically helps the local Romani community," says Ondřej Suchý, a representative of the company.
Last but not least, it is also worth mentioning the activity of the company Laundry and cleaning from the Karlovy Vary Region, which in the form of above-standard bonuses contributes to their pension insurance.
"In our country again, we give contributions for food, transport, improving qualifications and recreation," says Josef Strapáč from the Bruntál construction company Czasch, the winner in the Moravian-Silesian region.
All regional finalists of the Vodafone Company of the Year competition were automatically enjoined, who answered the questions of the questionnaire attached to the application and sent it no later than 15 August to the organizer, were automatically entered into the Responsible Company of the Year category.
Improperly completed or incomplete answers in the questionnaire were then eliminated by the organizer from the evaluation.
"Unless the representatives of the competitor of the company did not answer the questions, the Responsible Company of the Year competition could not participate, but are not disqualified from the "major" Vodafone Company of the Year competition."
"Separaate registration only for this competition is not possible, because it is a subcategory of the main competition Company of the Year," explains Karel Goldman from the organizing agency Bison & Rose.
