Cooper's companies, which collect $375 000 a month for their services that manage the company's run, $375 000 a month, will be rewarded for $4 million.
Barber and Birnbaum plan to rebuild production in MGM, which released only one film this year and put together a suggestion for seven or eight films that will come out in early 2012.
They also plan to participate in the financing of two films, the basis of which will be the book "Hobit", together with Warner Bros.
The studio needs to arrange a special loan between $2.65 million and $275 million in order to fund a stake in these two films, which will be directed by Peter Jackson.
