Romano goes after his first title
Rubén Omar Romano counts three defeats in the final, he experienced good and bad during his career, but he was already able to reach a decisive streak on three occasions.
in the duel of Santos Laguna and Monterrey in the final, two different styles will clash with their techniques, the teams who have a noticeable difference in the results.
Rubén Omar Romano counts three defeats in the final, during his career he experienced good and bad, but he was already able to reach the decisive streak on three occasions, but until now he has gone unaccompanied, and that's why this opportunity is extraordinary for him.
The Argentinian had to be satisfied with a silver medal, stayed step behind the winners, and quaintly played with the same team of the following final.
The Santist strategist as a coach got into his first final in the Apertura 2002 tournament when he was in the hands of the morelia club, with which he succumbed a total of 4-2 against Toluka; then he again advanced to a decisive duel in the Clausura 2003 tournament and also lost it with a total score of 3-1, which was against the Rayados team.
Already with the club Santos Laguna in the Torrneo Bicentenario 2010 tournament again against "The Devils" from Toluka, Rubén again suffered a defeat, although his team played against "Synars" (another nickname of the club Deportivo Toluca) after 210 minutes of the game indecisively 2-2, after a series of penalty shootouts he got into the advantage of three-on-one
Rubén already lost two finals against the "Black Devils" from Toluka and one against Monterrey, his future rival, so he would like to avoid the same fate and get rid of the curse, so he could celebrate the title for the first time, although he says the most important thing for him is an incumbent institution.
"I want to come out as a winner, I don't want to break the stats, this is for the club, for the passion I'm tied, and of course the title would also be for me, but the first is the most important thing," the coach commented when he was questioned about the numbers that speak in the final against him.
in viable memoir has a previous final, in which, as he confirms, he has learned a lot, "we have learned that until the referees whistle the end, we can't glorify, we have to be ready for action, as well as the players, because last time with the two pennies, we were already ready to run, and I don't think we've learned in this until the match is over, we can't celebrate."
Doesn't bother him that this series could be decided in penalty shootouts, he trusts his players: "You will never try to come to a series of penalty kicks, you are trying to finish in normal time, but sometimes there is no other option and it is necessary to be prepared for it, in the last tournament we were prepared, but unfortunately our fate has prepared a bad move, perhaps because of the nerves or anxiement that we felt when the title was in our hands."
Romano has in his hands a chance to stop being the latter and taste for the first time the fame that the titles bring.
U.S. Responds Rules for Visas
People will have to go back to services centers for visa applicants prior to an interview at the Consecutor's Office; the costs will be lower and the waiting time will be shortened.
From January 10, 2011, it will reschedule the process of discussing visas at the Embassy of the United States and consulates.
with a new procedure, most applicants will have to turn to Visa Applicant Services centres (absolute from ASC English) even before an interview at the Consular Department.
Personnel from the ASC removes the applicant's biometric information and these will be evaluated by the Consulate Department prior to the interview.
The new procedure will have certain advantages, among which are counting the following:
The total cost of separating the visa will be lower, it will no longer be necessary to pay a fee for the agreement of the meeting, the second for the processing of the application and another for the delivery of the document by the transport service.
The applicant will pay only a single fee, which will cover all three services.
The current fare will remain unaltered: an amount corresponding to $140 per tourist visa, $150 for visa cases applying (including visas for temporary workers) and $390 for a visa for traders and investors.
People wishing to rebuild their visa won’t have to hold an interview with a consular officer, but only turn to the nearest ASC, where they will present their papers and their fingerprints will be revoked.
Since biometric information will be withdrawn in the ASC, applicants who will require a second meeting with an Interview at the Consular Department will spend a shorter period of time here than in the past.
Likewise, those who will apply for a visa at consuliaments in Ciudad Juárez, Monterrey and Nuevo Laredo will no longer pay an extra service fee of $26.
For further information on the new visa application procedure, please visit http://mexico.usembassy.gov/boletines/sp101201_Visas-FAQs.html
NASA Announces Discovery of Alien Life
An U.S. space agency convened a press conference tomorrow to present a discovery that could wreave a turning point in search of extraterrestrial life.
The National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) of the United States will announce an astrobiological revival tomorrow that could confirm the theory of extraterrestrial life.
The revelation will be presented tomorrow by experts on astropiology, a science that deals with studying the origin, evolution, proliferation, and the future of life in the universe, at a press conference at NASA headquarters in Washington.
When she invited journalists, NASA reassured that it would introduce a "conceivation that will cause a turning point in the pursuit of extraterrestrial life," which sparked speculations of experts from other countries.
The discovery could confirm the theory that there are, in addition to us, other creatures living in inhospitable conditions that were considered uninhabitable, and which could represent the possibility that they will one day become intelligent creatures, such as humans, if the conditions in which they live improved.
According to appearances, it is a microbe that has been found at the bottom of Lake Mono in the Yosemist National Park in California, where it lives in an environment that was considered too poisonous for any form of life, as the lake is rich in arsenic.
Creature somehow uses arzen for its life, and it is this ability that increases the likelihood that such a life could exist on other planets that don’t have an atmosphere as on Earth.
According to astrobiologists, if these organisms use arsene in their metabolism, it will be proven that "there is a different form of life, different from the one we know".
The space agency will announce the true reach of the discoveries at tomorrow's press conference.
Geobiologist Pamela Conrad will take part in the conference, who studies the possibility of living on Mars; biologist Steven Benner, one of the scientists who examine Titan (Su Saturn's Greatest Month) with the prospect that its chemical composition is similar to that on Earth.
PRD, PT, Covergencia and Patron breed opposition "block"
The reforms of the Constitutional Law on Congress lead to the arrival of "bipartisanism", they declare.
It has not even been started the 60th parliamentary term when the opposition b bloc was formed in the Congress, led by the deputies of the parties PRD (Partido de la Revolución Democrática).
Prior to the start of the 60th parliamentary term, Felipe Manzanarez Rodríguez from Convergencia, Ezequiel Reynoso Esparza from PT, Javier Corvera Quevedo of PRD and Patrón Montalvo "thundered" against the reform of the Constitutional Act because he excludes them.
With this reform, they repeated, "bapartism" begins, because now it will be two persons from the same number of parties who will control Congress.
These four deputies, together with Gloria Margarita Santos Aquilar, coordinator of the PRD party, were the ones who voted against the Council, led by El Salvador Lóez Brito by PAN (Partido Acción) and Luis Cárdenas Fonseca as vice-president.
Corvera Quevedo stated that these reforms institutionally form political marginality at the instigation of the PRI (Partido Revolucionario Institucional, Czech "Revolutionary Institution Party").
He clarified that over the coming days they will speak with representatives of the PAN and PRI parties to modify the scheme on the basis of political will, and if they don't, they will again be subjugated by these two parties, ending the Opposition Coalition.
“As long as I got here (opposition coalition), I’m looking at it because we’re eliminated from any decision, they don’t even have a willingness to consider the opinions of the others.”
Felipe Manzanarez Rodríguez from Convergencia said they would coincide with PRD, PT and Patron and will therefore form a pluralistic group.
It is not possible to allow, he continued, so that Congress, after it has been monopolistic, would now be "duopial".
An aspiration to reform the law isn't to have endless bipartisanism in Congress.
This group begins with five legiscators, and its members are now talking to other colleagues and colleagues to get more votes, as Felipe Manzanarez Rodríguez added.
Ezekiel Reynoso Esparza from PT explained that at the moment Congress has become an "alcoke" of two - alluding to PAN and PRI parties.
"Previously there was only one side controlling it, today it is separated by two."
Patrón Montalvo demanded that he be reconsidered the personality of an MP to be given a seat at the negotiating table.
"So that the five deputies, of whom there will probably already be Nine of us, but right now they are seeing us in the top five because of the vaulted agreements, we have uneasied ourselves to find a seat at the negotiating table, because the problem is that in the reform that they have formed and agreed, we are standing outside, and we do not agree with this reform."
Another 200 Thousand Pesos for "Supplier"
The town hall in Mazatlán will pay for another cheque discussed to the owner of the company supplying electromaterial.
Another cheque for slightly more than 200 thousand pesos was dispatched to Lorena Guadalupe Camachová Palazuelos by the town hall.
Thus, the amount paid for in this second half-year to the owner of the company supplying electromaterial will rise to 1.200,000 pesos.
According to City Hall's Transparency page, this last cheque number 9258447 has been dispatched on November 16 this year, it was subject to 200.144.56 pesos and "equalising unpayable payments".
Treasurer Luis Miguel López Moreno remarked that the municipality will be paying this supplier, which has been pursued by the High State Revision Office due to the sale at high prices.
What has not been been said is the total amount still owed by the town hall, and how many cheques will still be shipped to Camach Palazuelos in favor of Camach Palazuelos.
“Nothing has been purchased right now, it is only paid for what we owe it, as well as other contractors,” he said in an interview.
The last cheques "reappeared again" in the last quarter of the year: September 24, two on October 15, October 19, October 29 and the last one on November 16.
Although this businesswowoman has not yet been published in the Government Paper, as stipulated in the case of companies audited by the High State Revision Office in order to preclude their services from being used by other administrative authorities, the Treasurer reassured that the services of the town hall did not re-educate.
At the previous time, after July 25, Noroeste published a review of cheques exhibited by the town hall to its contractors, which revealed that between March 2008 and July 9, during the three-year period of Mayor Jorge Abel López Sánchez, the city of Camach Palazuelos paid more than $10 million pesos through 42 cheques.
It also carried out transactions with Jumapam, where it collected cheques for more than 3 million pesos.
Hiking sites urgently need maintenance
Hiking managers are complaining in connection with an accident of a foreign tourist due to the poor condition of the Sánchez Taboada party in Mazatlán.
After the fall of a foreign hiker into the hollows-to-e-half Sánchze Taboady, the tourism sector in Mazatlan is asked by authorities to pay attention to areas and places that are in poor condition, thus not pointing the harbour in a good light.
Salvador Barraza Rubio, president of Zona Dorad Sales Association, recalled that they have repeatedly demanded the impression of the destination, the bad that tourists find here to be replaced by new activities or routes.
He argued that the misdemeanorence of the streets and sidewalks acts on tourists who are walking and seeing a clutter, which unfavorably affects nearby businesses.
"Politicians don't know what it's like to close a business for a day, and they don't have an idea of the sales they're leaking, otherwise they wouldn't have dealt with these issues so long and without proper planning."
Hotelier José Ramón Manguart Sánchez said the crash of the tourist caused a shortage of preventive measures and maintenance on the part of the town hall.
"The town hall will have to take responsibility and to avoid repeating something like this, it will have to devote itself to preventive maintenance, not just to repair pre-existing glitches," he said.
We would like to enjoy a clean city, because not only due to the fact that we are a tourist area should be maintained, after all, even as residents we deprive a clean residence, the town hall should change its city's maintenance strategy".
There are also other places that look negligible and miserable, he noted, such as the shrikan Emblem and El Venadito (monument, deer statue).
"Nowadays, in order for hikers to come, it doesn't just depend on promotion, it is necessary to offer a good product, that is, a city accompanies the purity of its beaches and allustrations, where the permanent maintenance of tourist attractions is carried out," he said.
"The necessary attention didn't pay attention to it, and these facts emphasize something that is well-known to everyone, maintenance is lacking.
Speaking about a number of places that need to be put in order in cooperation with the town hall, he said the priority must be to keep the city clean and in order for it to be attractive, because it has tourist potential.
Raúl Llera Martínez, sub-seater of the Tourist Graduation graduation, argued that rescuing tourist localities in Mazatlán is urgent, as they are not properly exploited and they do not make a good impression.
Luckily, Mazatlán offers many historical and cultural goals and spaces, but it will first have to be put in order to make these places more attractive and so that we can put them on the list we have to promote this destination."
IP Demands Results from Congress
Eduardo Dávalos, the CCE president, would like MPs to take a great tribute by setting an example in the search for a better Sinaloy, in the various challenges the state faces.
A parliamentary period full of dignified work and without agreements between the parties and the State executive is demanding the business sector in Mazatlan because Sinaloa convulses convulsions and faces major problems.
Since yesterday, the 60th parliamentary term has been launched, consisting of seven political forces, 19 PRI deputies, 13 from PAN, three on the Partido Nueva Alianza party, two from the PRD party, one of the PT, one from Convergencia's party and the last of PVEM, which includes a total of 40 national representatives.
On the list of expectations from the new members of Congress, it is for them to be able to implement decent leadership, with commitments to society and various areas that require responsible legislative work, and that the same party and paternalistic patrons will not be repeated.
Eduardo Dávalos Zamora, Chairman of the Coordinating Entrepreneurial Entrepreneurship (CCE), has proposed that the recently-elected 40 deputies of Congress should take a great responsibility and set an example on the path for a better Sinaloa with the various challenges he faces.
"We expect MPs to actually exercise their rights, without agreements between the parties, because they usually take measures to promote their own interests and become carnival processions of rulers and leaders of parliamentary factions."
That's why he talked about the need to reaffirm the commitment to the necessary brigadiers, which would move the ruling forward in order.
“We need them to do a dignified job and, above all, indebted to society and the sectors, because they were the inhabitants of Sinaloy who trusted them with their vote in the previous elections.”
José Ramón Manguart Sánchez, president of Tres Isslas hotel association, said that one of the biggest challenges for 40 national representatives will be to gather all the forces in an quest to achieve the economic growth of the country, because the current economic situation is very complex.
The most important thing is to insulate economic growth, to create incentives for investment and infrastructure, which will intensify jobs in a certain way.
Regarding tourism, he demanded that the new legislators give him more weight within the state budget and support the Ministry of Tourism.
"I've learned that it's a ministry with the second-highest budget, which is disproportionate given that it's an important economic activity, bringing currencies and investments, which, moreover, directly compete with agriculture."
In addition, in order to expend funds for start-up tourism projects, Congress should help supply the state at certainty and assistance with the Alcohol Act, which has not been handled in previous parliamentary terms.
They are looking for the Three Kings
Dolls, cars and bicycles, along with other toys, are on the children's wish list in the Coronad Valenzuel family.
It will be difficult for their parents to fulfill their ideas on the upcoming feast of the Three Kings, as their household counts exactly 12 people and one rake.
But Adelaida, Isabel, Jesús, José Alfredo, María Guadalupe, Isaías, José Juan and Miguel do not lose the hope that Kašpar, Melichar and Baltazar will give them the toys and clothes they desire so much.
The family lives in a modest dwelling of Colonia Salvador Allende in poor circumstances as his father doesn't have a permanent job.
"Sometimes we have a hard time because my husband doesn't have any luck, but we sell mandarins and potatoes... In the afternoon I'm going out with "pedbeians" on the street selling on the street," said Cayetana Valenzuel Andrade, the children's mother.
Four-year-old Adelaida wants a do doll or a bike while her three-year-old sister Isabel would have liked the Barbie doll.
As far as ten-year-old José Alfred is concerned, he would have wanted a "monster" car for some time, and for his eight-month-a-half-year-old Jesús, Cayetana would have wanted one-a-half-year-old.
“Knowed me (José Alfredo) ‘who want this monster car,’ but I told him ‘we’re going to ‘save a son’ because it was very expensive,” Cayetano recalled.
For older children who were just at school, clothes and shoes would be ideal.
María Guadalupe, who is 11 years old, has the size of a 12-year-old Isaías the size 10, while eight-year-old Miguel wears a size 8.
The fourteen-year-old José Juan lacks sneakers, so he'd be very comfortable with a five-and-and-a-half-and-six-emilar pair.
If you would like to help fulfill the dreams of children from the Coronad Valenzuel family, you can take part in the "Search for the Three Kings" campaign, and bring a gift or money in cash at the reception of Noroeste.
